{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Suvdb6DSq8ufR9oWpk2EyP","type":"tool_result","content":"55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n271:- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n295:- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n331:- `input.mouse`: { cx, cy } its page position, active once it has moved over the canvas, t the input clock when it last moved\n338:- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n340:- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n1064:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1340:- `E.FIGHT_KEYS: up, down, left, right, lp, hp, lk, hk, start, pause, confirm, cancel` †: the fighting preset (a scene's input): the moves and menu keys of E.Input.DEFAULT, light and heavy punch (U, I; a pad's X, Y), light and heavy kick (J, K; A, B)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"2925d8c8-18b1-4b99-8a4b-e6e49058e065","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:29:01.555Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n271:- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pix