{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyKxEcNtdbU3cLLCC8Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XTHFxj7HxueRNzt3WvkWhU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"^- \\`E.rng\\|E.ik3\\|^- \\`E.tones\\|^- \\`E.store\\|^- \\`E.arc\\b\\|^- \\`E.addAssets\\|^- \\`E.shape\\b\\|^- \\`r.queue\\|^- \\`r.shape\\|^- \\`r.box\\|^- \\`game.menu(\\|^- \\`game.saves\\|^- \\`game.allowJoin\\|^- \\`game.addPlayer\\|^- \\`game.script\\|^- \\`E.until\\|^- \\`r.glowDisc\\|^- \\`r.groundRing\\|^- \\`r.groundDisc\\|^- \\`r.decal\\|^- \\`px.blend\\|^- \\`r.prop\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-330","description":"Look up signatures for helpers to use"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5539,"cache_read_input_tokens":199990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5539},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"b13dc1ca-92aa-4242-84f1-21bb61d017c0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:33:17.631Z","request_id":"req_011CghyKwyVBpnCJk2KjhQgi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XTHFxj7HxueRNzt3WvkWhU":{"command":"grep -n \"^- \\`E.rng\\|E.ik3\\|^- \\`E.tones\\|^- \\`E.store\\|^- \\`E.arc\\b\\|^- \\`E.addAssets\\|^- \\`E.shape\\b\\|^- \\`r.queue\\|^- \\`r.shape\\|^- \\`r.box\\|^- \\`game.menu(\\|^- \\`game.saves\\|^- \\`game.allowJoin\\|^- \\`game.addPlayer\\|^- \\`game.script\\|^- \\`E.until\\|^- \\`r.glowDisc\\|^- \\`r.groundRing\\|^- \\`r.groundDisc\\|^- \\`r.decal\\|^- \\`px.blend\\|^- \\`r.prop\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-330","description":"Look up signatures for helpers to use"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTHFxj7HxueRNzt3WvkWhU","type":"tool_result","content":"135:- `E.arc(a, b, g, o = {})` †: the throw from a to b ({ x, y, z }) under gravity g (units a second squared, pulling z down): a lob to a teammate's feet, a grenade, a leap to a ledge. o: { apex: how far it rises over the higher end (24), or time: the seconds it flies, or speed: a launch speed (the lower arc that reaches; null \n165:- `E.ik3(a, b, L1, L2, hint)`: two-bone IK in 3D: returns [joint, end]. hint points the way the joint should bend.\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n415:- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a stat\n428:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing e\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a genera\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a \n599:- `E.until(fn)` †: a script's wait until fn() is true: yield E.until(() => door.open)\n1095:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Re","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"bbba41cc-0891-4b74-b3f1-f8c559a4e8b0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:33:17.652Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"135:- `E.arc(a, b, g, o = {})` †: the throw from a to b ({ x, y, z }) under gravity g (units a second squared, pulling z down): a lob to a teammate's feet, a grenade, a leap to a ledge. o: { apex: how far it rises over the higher end (24), or time: the seconds it flies, or speed: a launch speed (the lower arc that reaches; null \n165:- `E.ik3(a, b, L1, L2, hint)`: two-bone IK in 3D: returns [joint, end]. hint points the way the joint should bend.\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n197:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n415:- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a stat\n428:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing e\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a genera\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a \n599:- `E.until(fn)` †: a script's wait until fn() is true: yield E.until(() => door.open)\n1095:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Re","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XTHFxj7HxueRNzt3WvkWhU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
