{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dz5bguwrEgNujTqAZgyZ1X","type":"tool_result","content":"282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n306:- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n470:- `game.after(seconds, fn)`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change. Returns { cancel() }\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking \n491:- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"4ffeb6ec-f3ca-46fa-8fcd-019e1a08cc22","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:12:51.003Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n306:- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n470:- `game.after(seconds, fn)`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change. Returns { cancel() }\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking \n491:- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dz5bguwrEgNujTqAZgyZ1X","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
