{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5fQoVccKumWWEsDbXu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The round runs identically in both harness copies. Small fix for the Ready button label, then the design notes, final feedback text and the exit interview:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1964,"cache_read_input_tokens":707092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1964},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"e0fbee5c-2aaa-4912-b625-1826f696f48f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:55:37.479Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5fQMxy64ksttgQu8Z5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5fQoVccKumWWEsDbXu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N4urTsUUfbFoJEk3vxXyA5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef rep(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read(); assert a in s, a[:60]; s=s.replace(a,b,1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nrep('src/54-hub.js',\"E.font.text(g, 'READY', this.btns[0][0] + bw / 2 + 6, H - 38,\",\"E.font.text(g, 'READY', this.btns[0][0] + bw / 2 + 14, H - 38,\")\nrep('src/54-hub.js',\"E.font.text(g, 'MORE TIME', this.btns[1][0] + bw / 2 + 6, H - 38,\",\"E.font.text(g, 'MORE TIME', this.btns[1][0] + bw / 2 + 8, H - 38,\")\np='src/56-feedback.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s[s.index('ABOUT.testingFeedback = ['):s.index('ABOUT.engineFeedback')]\nb='''ABOUT.testingFeedback = [\n  'About 41 issues: 25 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual or layout problems, 6 balance problems (wides, a passive CPU batter, a slow sandy outfield) and a few test-harness mistakes of my own.',\n  '8 were game breaking: a dead ball that never ended (a review timer below zero), two scenes that could only finish once (stale flags), a misnamed dead-ball handler, the camera pointed thousands of units away (radians read as degrees), an engine floor-bake crash at the low broadcast pitch, long throws counted as overthrows (15-second balls), and a commentary crash in CPU-only matches.',\n  'The forced-outcome scenarios (sim-field, sim-arcade, attract): they drive the real delivery director end to end, and found most of the logic bugs and all the stuck-ball ones.',\n  'The solved-delivery accuracy check: it mostly measured the 1/120 s step quantization of the pitching point, not a game bug.'\n];\n'''\ns=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > DESIGN-NOTES.md <<'EOF'\n# Cricket Kerfuffle: design notes (how to add content)\n\nEverything is data keyed by id; systems look things up and never need editing for new content.\n\n- **A team**: add an entry to `TEAMS` in `src/10-data.js` (code, kit colours, a name pool, 3-5 stars with `bat pow tech\n  fld ctc`, `bowl: { del: [3 delivery ids], skill }`, `sp` batting special, `bsp` bowling special, `voice`, `look` rig\n  options). `squad()` fills it to eleven from the pool. Add its portrait voice to `VOICES` if it speaks in the story.\n- **A ground**: add a `GROUNDS` entry (boundary `rx ry`, pitch factors, outfield decay, palette, sky, `targets` with\n  position, radius, bonus and commentary line, a `chaos` pool), then its buildings in `groundRecipe()` and its props in\n  `groundProps()` (`src/30-art.js`). The panorama (`panoramaFor`) paints itself from the palette and `surround`.\n- **A delivery**: add to `DELIVERIES` (family, km/h range, swing, seam, turn, bounce, length band). Give it to a bowler's\n  `bowl.del`. The CPU aims inside its swing and turn by itself.\n- **A shot**: add a row to `SHOTS` (button, lengths, sector, animation family, `at` contact time, launch, speed, zone).\n  The resolver picks it; the animation family's keyframes live in `BAT_KEYS` (`src/31-cast.js`).\n- **A special**: add to `SPECIALS`, then its effect in `_release` (bowling) or `_contact` (batting) in `src/22-play.js`.\n- **A chaos event**: add to `CHAOS` and to a ground's pool; give it a start in `triggerChaos`, any per-step behaviour in\n  `chaosStep`/`chaosBall`, and an end in `endChaos` (`src/25-chaos.js`).\n- **A story chapter**: add to `CHAPTERS` (`src/11-data-story.js`): opponent, ground, overs, an optional `scenario`\n  (start in the second innings), `pre`/`mid`/`win` lines as `[speaker, text]` (`'*'` is a caption), and three goals as\n  `[label, match => bool]`. Add a pin to `MAP_PINS`.\n- **A commentary line**: add `[speaker, text]` to a pool in `LINES`; templates `{batter} {bowler} {team} {ground} ...`.\n- **A lesson**: add to `LESSONS` (`src/51-match-scene.js`): the role, a goal count, the bus events to listen to and a\n  check, two lines of Mrs Crumb's instructions.\n- **An attract segment**: add to `SEGMENTS` (`src/52-attract.js`): ground, teams, a chaos event, and balls as forced\n  outcomes (`six four one dot edge bowled caught lbw runout stumped`, plus `target`, `th`, `special`, `bat`).\n- **Tuning**: every live variable is in `TUNE_DEFS` (`src/00-core.js`) and shows as a dev-mode slider at once.\n\nBuild: `node tools/build.mjs`. Test: `node test/run.mjs [suite ...]`. Balance report: `node test/balance.mjs`.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs -q && node test/run.mjs unit-rules sim-front bundle 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Hub button label, final testing feedback, design notes","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1964,"cache_read_input_tokens":707092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1964},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"d12dde6c-894c-427f-ba25-433ed705a45c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:55:53.818Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5fQMxy64ksttgQu8Z5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01N4urTsUUfbFoJEk3vxXyA5":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef rep(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read(); assert a in s, a[:60]; s=s.replace(a,b,1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nrep('src/54-hub.js',\"E.font.text(g, 'READY', this.btns[0][0] + bw / 2 + 6, H - 38,\",\"E.font.text(g, 'READY', this.btns[0][0] + bw / 2 + 14, H - 38,\")\nrep('src/54-hub.js',\"E.font.text(g, 'MORE TIME', this.btns[1][0] + bw / 2 + 6, H - 38,\",\"E.font.text(g, 'MORE TIME', this.btns[1][0] + bw / 2 + 8, H - 38,\")\np='src/56-feedback.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s[s.index('ABOUT.testingFeedback = ['):s.index('ABOUT.engineFeedback')]\nb='''ABOUT.testingFeedback = [\n  'About 41 issues: 25 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual or layout problems, 6 balance problems (wides, a passive CPU batter, a slow sandy outfield) and a few test-harness mistakes of my own.',\n  '8 were game breaking: a dead ball that never ended (a review timer below zero), two scenes that could only finish once (stale flags), a misnamed dead-ball handler, the camera pointed thousands of units away (radians read as degrees), an engine floor-bake crash at the low broadcast pitch, long throws counted as overthrows (15-second balls), and a commentary crash in CPU-only matches.',\n  'The forced-outcome scenarios (sim-field, sim-arcade, attract): they drive the real delivery director end to end, and found most of the logic bugs and all the stuck-ball ones.',\n  'The solved-delivery accuracy check: it mostly measured the 1/120 s step quantization of the pitching point, not a game bug.'\n];\n'''\ns=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > DESIGN-NOTES.md <<'EOF'\n# Cricket Kerfuffle: design notes (how to add content)\n\nEverything is data keyed by id; systems look things up and never need editing for new content.\n\n- **A team**: add an entry to `TEAMS` in `src/10-data.js` (code, kit colours, a name pool, 3-5 stars with `bat pow tech\n  fld ctc`, `bowl: { del: [3 delivery ids], skill }`, `sp` batting special, `bsp` bowling special, `voice`, `look` rig\n  options). `squad()` fills it to eleven from the pool. Add its portrait voice to `VOICES` if it speaks in the story.\n- **A ground**: add a `GROUNDS` entry (boundary `rx ry`, pitch factors, outfield decay, palette, sky, `targets` with\n  position, radius, bonus and commentary line, a `chaos` pool), then its buildings in `groundRecipe()` and its props in\n  `groundProps()` (`src/30-art.js`). The panorama (`panoramaFor`) paints itself from the palette and `surround`.\n- **A delivery**: add to `DELIVERIES` (family, km/h range, swing, seam, turn, bounce, length band). Give it to a bowler's\n  `bowl.del`. The CPU aims inside its swing and turn by itself.\n- **A shot**: add a row to `SHOTS` (button, lengths, sector, animation family, `at` contact time, launch, speed, zone).\n  The resolver picks it; the animation family's keyframes live in `BAT_KEYS` (`src/31-cast.js`).\n- **A special**: add to `SPECIALS`, then its effect in `_release` (bowling) or `_contact` (batting) in `src/22-play.js`.\n- **A chaos event**: add to `CHAOS` and to a ground's pool; give it a start in `triggerChaos`, any per-step behaviour in\n  `chaosStep`/`chaosBall`, and an end in `endChaos` (`src/25-chaos.js`).\n- **A story chapter**: add to `CHAPTERS` (`src/11-data-story.js`): opponent, ground, overs, an optional `scenario`\n  (start in the second innings), `pre`/`mid`/`win` lines as `[speaker, text]` (`'*'` is a caption), and three goals as\n  `[label, match => bool]`. Add a pin to `MAP_PINS`.\n- **A commentary line**: add `[speaker, text]` to a pool in `LINES`; templates `{batter} {bowler} {team} {ground} ...`.\n- **A lesson**: add to `LESSONS` (`src/51-match-scene.js`): the role, a goal count, the bus events to listen to and a\n  check, two lines of Mrs Crumb's instructions.\n- **An attract segment**: add to `SEGMENTS` (`src/52-attract.js`): ground, teams, a chaos event, and balls as forced\n  outcomes (`six four one dot edge bowled caught lbw runout stumped`, plus `target`, `th`, `special`, `bat`).\n- **Tuning**: every live variable is in `TUNE_DEFS` (`src/00-core.js`) and shows as a dev-mode slider at once.\n\nBuild: `node tools/build.mjs`. Test: `node test/run.mjs [suite ...]`. Balance report: `node test/balance.mjs`.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs -q && node test/run.mjs unit-rules sim-front bundle 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Hub button label, final testing feedback, design notes","timeout":300000}}}
