{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5y4VdEryA9R2RufEKG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built **Cricket Kerfuffle**, an over-the-top arcade cricket game, as the single file `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-062757.html` in this folder's root, with `exit-interview.json` beside it. It opens from file:// with no network requests. The final full run of `node test/run.mjs` gave **275 passed, 0 failed (16 suites)**; the browser suite (including the AI Hub harness) was run once more after a last fix to its server cleanup and passed again. The working files are in the `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-…-062757/` subfolder.\n\n**What's in it**\n- **Modes:** a 5-chapter story (prologue, cutscenes with portraits and gibberish voices, a story map, 3 stars per chapter, an ending and credits), Quick Match with a toss, Versus for 2–4 players on one screen, Super Over Showdown (bat or bowl) with high-score tables, and the Nets (11 lessons, free practice, the Six Machine).\n- **Cricket:** timed and aimed batting with 20 shots, bowling with a target marker, a release meter, aftertouch and field presets, running with calls and dives, fielding with a catch ring and throws, all the ways to get out, and reviews with an Owl-Eye replay and a third umpire.\n- **Arcade layer:** the Hype meter, ON FIRE streaks, 21 character specials, items, stadium targets and 15 chaos events (rain with a revised target, tide, fog, ghosts and more).\n- **Required extras:**\n  - **Attract mode:** a 10-segment showreel after 10 s idle; any input exits.\n  - **Dev mode:** reached from the pause menu, with 33 live sliders and a reset, toggles, and jumps (forced outcomes, chapters, chaos events).\n  - **Controls:** PlayStation glyphs by default with Xbox in Settings; keys, mouse and pad all native.\n  - **Touch-only devices:** they get the \"Controller or keyboard required\" screen with a Settings button, and the attract mode still runs.\n  - **AI Hub:** a parallel Super Over for 1–4 players with the game's own card.\n  - **About/Credits:** pages carrying the four sections below.\n\n**Changes from the plan**\n- The rain-delay formula scales by total resources, not the plan's simpler version.\n- Chapter 3's chase is 26, not 30, so it's winnable.\n- Batter run speed defaults to 135, not 120.\n- The CPU plays through \"virtual pads\" (it presses the same buttons a player would).\n- The new art lives in the engine's shape table rather than a separate asset file.\n\n**Not checked:** I had no real gamepad or touch device; those paths were tested only through simulated input. Gameplay balance was tuned from CPU-vs-CPU statistics and screenshots, not hands-on play.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:27:57\n- **Source:** Cricket (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign. 2.5D in projected-3D views: a TV-style camera behind the bowler for every delivery, a high wide camera following the ball, close-ups, and a side-on review camera. Story scenes use a three-quarter view.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node and Playwright 1.63.0.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's pixel-art character style at 320×240 (expanded to fill the screen), canvas lighting, engine shapes and materials, plus new cricket assets: stumps, sight screens, the pub, church, greenhouse, Ferris wheel, top hat, jumbotron, the Thrumptonator, Doris the cow, and a painted far-end view of the stands.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character rigs, plus a cricket layer that reposes the joints (IK): two-handed bat swings by shot family, an overarm bowling action, umpire signals, catches and keeping; engine throws, poses and dives.\n- **Audio:** Chip-synth music in layers (drums come in with the Hype meter, a fire layer when ON FIRE), synthesized effects, a crowd engine (murmur, applause, roars, chant) and Animalese-style gibberish voices. All in code, no audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1: a parallel Super Over at the Megadome for 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\n- **Testing:** Headless engine (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), scripted playthroughs and CPU bot matches behind one command, Playwright browser checks, the AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** None beyond the plan, the engine's handoff docs and kits, and the AI Hub README and example.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 41: 25 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual or layout problems, 6 balance problems (too many wides, a passive CPU batter, a slow sandy outfield), and a few mistakes in my own tests.\n- **How many were critical / game breaking?** 8:\n  - a dead ball that never ended (a review timer went below zero);\n  - two scenes (cutscenes and the match) that could only finish once, because of leftover flags;\n  - a misnamed dead-ball handler;\n  - the camera pointed thousands of units away (degrees read as radians);\n  - an engine crash drawing the ground at the low TV-camera angle;\n  - long throws counted as overthrows, making balls last 15 s;\n  - a commentary crash in CPU-only matches.\n- **Most helpful test:** The forced-outcome scenarios (sim-field, sim-arcade, attract). They run the real ball-by-ball machinery end to end, and found most of the logic bugs and all of the stuck balls.\n- **Least helpful test:** The check that bowled balls land where they were aimed. It mostly measured the simulation's 1/120 s step size, not a game bug.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The character rig: a dressed, lit, animated cricketer from one options object. Its pose step is open to wrapping, so bat swings and a bowling action could be added with IK.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. A custom camera view stores its pitch in radians (`pitchDeg` holds the degrees), which put the camera thousands of units away. In a headless test, a long press made the click check come back empty.\n- **Most important thing you built yourself:** The cricket itself: ball physics and its predictor, the ball-by-ball flow, fielding and running, umpiring and reviews, and the forced-outcome layer that the attract mode and dev mode share.\n- **Hardest part:** Framing a strongly foreshortened TV camera. The ground drawing broke at a low angle, and the far end needed a painted backdrop of the stands.\n- **What did you change, and why?** A cricket bat with a two-handed grip; batting pads; moustaches, beards and glasses; PlayStation glyphs by default with Xbox as the option; Create + Options left to the AI Hub; ten cached ground drawings (was six); and a fix for a crash when trimming the ground-drawing cache. All are logged in `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md`.\n- **One change you'd make:** A perspective (telephoto) camera option for ground views, so a TV-style sports camera doesn't need a painted backdrop for the far end.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The clear, testable definition of done, and the freedom to change the engine.\n- **What was confusing?** How much of a very large plan is binding when TASK.md says it wins on disagreements, and what \"follow\" means for the plan versus the AI Hub protocol.\n- **Hardest thing to do?** Fitting a full cricket simulation, five grounds, a story, local and online multiplayer, an attract mode and a dev mode into one session, with honest testing.\n- **What would you change?** Give a target scope (minutes of play, number of modes) and say which plan features are required and which are optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":718038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"14e1f70a-3c9c-4ce5-bd08-f9ed0957d0a2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:59:51.044Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5y42Lqhq8LHqc2ZGo1"}
