{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi7LyQ1RT671hmLGMbZ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The three plan deviations are gone: the game now uses the plan's exact values and formula, and everything still passes — **296 of 296 checks across 17 suites**. The game file and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, the interview parses with every field answered, and no server I started is still running.\n\n**Back to the plan:**\n- **Rain delay:** the revised target uses the plan's formula, floor(first-innings runs × R_after / R_before) + 1, never less than the current score + 1. The rules test checks the plan's numbers: 30 is revised to 16 off 2 overs.\n- **Chapter 3:** the chase is back to the plan's 30 runs (the Larrikins make 29).\n- **Run speed:** the batters' default is back to the plan's 120.\n\nTo keep chapter 3 winnable at 30, the CPU batter swings at nearly everything in reach once it needs more than 10 an over. The autopilot that plays for a human side (the campaign test, dev Auto-bat) now has a smaller timing error. The story campaign is still won chapter by chapter through to the credits. The rain-delay formula, chapter 3's chase and the run speed now match PLAN.md; the build choices listed earlier (CPU virtual pads, the cricket art in the engine's shape table) still stand.\n\n**What the evidence is, and its limits:**\n- **Features:** every TASK.md feature and every plan system is in the game, with no TODOs or stubs. 296 checks exercise them, from the build file name through all 21 special effects, the story ending, attract mode, dev mode, the touch-only screen and the AI Hub harness with 1, 2 and 4 players.\n- **Input:** touch, gamepad and mouse go through Chromium's own input channels, but on emulated devices. I have no physical controller or touch screen here.\n- **Independence:** the tests are mine. TASK.md rules out using subagents to review or audit, so I have no outside check beyond the AI Hub harness's own conformance test.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:27:57\n- **Source:** Cricket (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign. A TV camera behind the bowler for every delivery, a wide camera that follows the ball, close-ups and a side-on review camera, and a three-quarter view for story scenes.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node and Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's pixel-art characters at 320×240 (expanded to fill the screen), canvas lighting, engine shapes and materials, and new cricket assets.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, posed by IK for two-handed bat swings, the overarm bowling action and umpire signals.\n- **Audio:** Music in layers, synthesized effects, a crowd engine and Animalese-style gibberish voices, all made in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1: a parallel Super Over for 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\n- **Testing:** The headless engine (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), scripted playthroughs and CPU bot matches behind one command, Playwright browser checks (including emulated touch, gamepad and mouse input), and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** None beyond the plan, the engine's handoff docs and kits, and the AI Hub README and example.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 42: roughly 26 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual, 6 balance, and a few errors in my own tests.\n2. **How many were critical?** 8:\n   - a dead ball that never ended;\n   - two scenes that could only finish once;\n   - a misnamed dead-ball handler;\n   - the camera aimed far off the ground;\n   - an engine crash drawing the ground at the low camera angle;\n   - long throws counted as overthrows;\n   - a commentary crash in CPU-only matches.\n3. **Most helpful test:** The forced-outcome scenarios, which run the real ball-by-ball machinery end to end.\n4. **Least helpful test:** The check that deliveries land where aimed, which mostly measured the simulation's step size.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The character rig; its pose step can be wrapped to add IK.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** A custom view keeps its pitch in radians (`pitchDeg` holds degrees). In a headless test, a long press left the click check empty.\n3. **Built myself:** The cricket simulation, fielding and running, umpiring and reviews, and the forced-outcome layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** The low TV camera: the ground drawing broke at that angle, and the far end needed a painted backdrop.\n5. **Changed:**\n   - a cricket bat with a two-handed grip;\n   - batting pads, moustaches, beards and glasses;\n   - PlayStation glyphs by default, with Xbox as the option;\n   - Create + Options left to the AI Hub;\n   - ten cached ground drawings instead of six;\n   - a fix for the ground-drawing cache crash.\n6. **One change:** A perspective (telephoto) camera option for ground views.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The testable definition of done, and the freedom to change the engine.\n2. **Confusing:** How binding a very large plan is when TASK.md wins on disagreements.\n3. **Hardest:** Fitting the full game and its testing into one session.\n4. **Would change:** Give a target scope, and say which plan features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":744192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":719,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"eed45c73-4945-484c-bd68-bf4a2c08bca0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:17:44.523Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7Ly1wocMhb1D3cPmZo"}
