{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi7eb8pMhruaZ3yCGcsA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**296 of 296 checks pass across 17 suites** after the last change. `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-062757.html` and `exit-interview.json` (which parses, every field answered) are in this folder's root. No server I started is still running.\n\nThis round I looked directly at the two items the hook kept naming instead of just re-running tests:\n\n- **The story ending:** after the final chapter, the \"THE END\" scene plays. Lord Thrumpton asks for one exhibition ball against the vicar, is given out leg before again and finally laughs, tears up the deeds, and the ghosts leave. It goes on to the credits page, closing on \"Lord Thrumpton-Vane is adequate at fine leg.\" I took screenshots of both in Chromium (`test/out/ending.png`, `test/out/credits.png`), and the campaign test reaches them by playing all five chapters.\n- **The two specials:**\n  - Dibbly-Dobbly Doom bowls an 80 km/h ball that wobbles in the air and doubles the CPU batter's timing error, which is what the plan describes.\n  - Sawn in Half is a googly, and a bowled wicket now visibly splits the stumps: a gold saw cut, the two halves sliding apart, sawdust in the air. Before, it was only a thin line. The side-on capture is in `test/out/sheet_sawn.png`.\n  - Both effects are checked in the arcade test, alongside the other 19 specials.\n- **Matching the plan:** the rain-delay formula, chapter 3's 30-run chase and the batters' run speed now match PLAN.md exactly.\n\nWhat can't be shown from here:\n\n- **Real devices:** touch, gamepad and mouse were tested through Chromium's own input channels on emulated devices. There is no physical controller or touch screen on this machine.\n- **Independent review:** the tests and the visual checks are mine. TASK.md rules out using subagents to review or audit, and the only outside check is the AI Hub harness's own conformance test, which passes with 1, 2 and 4 players.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:27:57\n- **Source:** Cricket (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign. A TV camera behind the bowler for every delivery, a wide camera that follows the ball, close-ups and a side-on review camera; story scenes use a three-quarter view.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node and Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's pixel-art characters at 320×240 (expanded to fill the screen), canvas lighting, engine shapes and materials, and new cricket assets.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, posed by IK for two-handed bat swings, the overarm bowling action and umpire signals.\n- **Audio:** Music in layers, synthesized effects, a crowd engine and Animalese-style gibberish voices, all made in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1: a parallel Super Over for 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\n- **Testing:** The headless engine (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), scripted playthroughs and CPU bot matches behind one command, Playwright browser checks (including emulated touch, gamepad and mouse input), and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** None beyond the plan, the engine's handoff docs and kits, and the AI Hub README and example.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 42: roughly 26 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual problems, 6 balance problems and a few errors in my own tests.\n2. **How many were critical?** 8:\n   - a dead ball that never ended;\n   - two scenes that could only finish once;\n   - a misnamed dead-ball handler;\n   - the camera aimed far off the ground;\n   - an engine crash drawing the ground at the low camera angle;\n   - long throws counted as overthrows;\n   - a commentary crash in CPU-only matches.\n3. **Most helpful test:** The forced-outcome scenarios, which run the real ball-by-ball machinery end to end.\n4. **Least helpful test:** The check that deliveries land where aimed; it mostly measured the simulation's step size.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The character rig; its pose step can be wrapped to add IK.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** A custom view keeps its pitch in radians (`pitchDeg` holds the degrees). In a headless test, a long press left the click check empty.\n3. **Built myself:** The cricket simulation, fielding and running, umpiring and reviews, and the forced-outcome layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** The low TV camera: the ground drawing broke at that angle, and the far end needed a painted backdrop.\n5. **Changed:**\n   - a cricket bat with a two-handed grip;\n   - batting pads, moustaches, beards and glasses;\n   - PlayStation glyphs by default, with Xbox as the option;\n   - Create + Options left to the AI Hub;\n   - ten cached ground drawings instead of six;\n   - a fix for the ground-drawing cache crash.\n6. **One change:** A perspective (telephoto) camera option for ground views.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The testable definition of done, and the freedom to change the engine.\n2. **Confusing:** How binding a very large plan is when TASK.md wins on disagreements.\n3. **Hardest:** Fitting the full game and its testing into one session.\n4. **Would change:** Give a target scope, and say which plan features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":754818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":431},"output_tokens":741,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"d13f15e4-f289-4be3-95cd-75db306c6515","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:21:42.489Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7eamyZscJBoTp8yU9i"}
