{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi7tPsn3j7WSSuGCygsK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a structural completeness suite, and it found unused content that the word grep had missed. I wired all of it in; the full run is now **307 passed, 0 failed (18 suites)**.\n\n**What the new suite checks** (it runs as part of `node test/run.mjs`):\n- No method or event handler in the source has an empty body.\n- Every special, item and chaos event in the game's data has code that runs it.\n- Every game setting is read by the game.\n- Every commentary pool, sound effect, song and sting is played somewhere.\n- Every scene exists and can be reached.\n\n**What it caught, now fixed:**\n- The free-hit and Kerfuffle-bonus commentary lines were never spoken. They now play after those balls.\n- The splash sound was never played. It now plays when the ball lands in the fountain, the water tower or the inflatable shark.\n- The steam sound was never played. It now plays as the Thrumptonator winds up.\n\nThe single file `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-062757.html` and `exit-interview.json` (parses, every field answered) are in this folder's root, and no server I started is still running. Two things are still not possible here: a physical gamepad or touch screen (the tests use Chromium's emulated devices), and an independent review (TASK.md rules out subagents for that).\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:27:57\n- **Source:** Cricket (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign. A TV camera behind the bowler for every delivery, a wide camera following the ball, close-ups and a side-on review camera; story scenes use a three-quarter view.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node and Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's pixel-art characters at 320×240, expanded to fill the screen, with canvas lighting, engine shapes and materials, and new cricket assets.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, posed by IK for two-handed bat swings, the overarm bowling action and umpire signals.\n- **Audio:** Layered music, synthesized effects, a crowd engine and Animalese-style gibberish voices, all made in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1: a parallel Super Over for 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\n- **Testing:** Headless engine (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), scripted playthroughs and CPU bot matches behind one command, Playwright browser checks (including emulated touch, gamepad and mouse input), and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** None beyond the plan, the engine's handoff docs and kits, and the AI Hub README and example.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 46: roughly 26 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual problems, 6 balance problems, 4 unused pieces of content found by the structural scan, and a few errors in my own tests.\n2. **How many were critical?** 8:\n   - a dead ball that never ended\n   - two scenes that could only finish once\n   - a misnamed dead-ball handler\n   - the camera aimed far off the ground\n   - an engine crash drawing the ground at the low camera angle\n   - long throws counted as overthrows\n   - a commentary crash in CPU-only matches\n3. **Most helpful test:** The forced-outcome scenarios, which run the real ball-by-ball code end to end.\n4. **Least helpful test:** The check that deliveries land where aimed; it mostly measured the simulation's step size.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The character rig; its pose step can be wrapped to add IK.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** A custom view stores its pitch in radians (`pitchDeg` holds the degrees). In a headless test, a long press left the click check empty.\n3. **Built myself:** The cricket simulation, fielding, running, umpiring and reviews, and the forced-outcome layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** The low TV camera: the ground drawing broke at that angle, and the far end needed a painted backdrop.\n5. **Changed:**\n   - a cricket bat with a two-handed grip\n   - batting pads, moustaches, beards and glasses\n   - PlayStation glyphs by default, with Xbox as the option\n   - Create + Options left to the AI Hub\n   - ten cached ground drawings instead of six\n   - a fix for the ground-drawing cache crash\n6. **One change:** A perspective (telephoto) camera option for ground views.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The testable definition of done, and the freedom to change the engine.\n2. **Confusing:** How binding a very large plan is when TASK.md wins on disagreements.\n3. **Hardest:** Fitting the full game and its testing into one session.\n4. **Would change:** Give a target scope, and say which plan features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":763249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":354},"output_tokens":734,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"18763c2b-c43c-49fb-93bc-3e0ad0934bad","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:24:47.737Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7tPVxtjYo3qG2Ht9ck"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The file, exit-interview.json and the four sections are present, but the condition requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented with no stubs, and the transcript doesn't establish that. The no-stub evidence is a TODO/FIXME/placeholder grep plus a structural scan the assistant wrote, which it found gaps with only after the stop hook had repeatedly flagged them. Real gamepad and touch input were never tested (only emulated input), and no independent review was done. The assistant's last message also says these checks can't be completed here."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"b3e3d3ee-4bcf-4f5c-87ae-81afd9a4a12d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:24:50.263Z","isSynthetic":true}
