{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi7vzrn1tcjPPq95ABrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game hasn't changed: all 307 checks across 18 suites pass, and the game file `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-062757.html` and `exit-interview.json` (which parses, with every field answered) are in this folder's root.\n\nThe two remaining objections can't be met from here:\n\n- **Real devices:** this headless machine has no physical gamepad or touch screen. Those inputs were tested only through Chromium's emulated devices.\n- **Independent review:** TASK.md forbids subagents for review or audit, so I'm the only reviewer available. The AI Hub harness's conformance check, which passes, is the only outside check.\n\nI'll stop adding verification passes, because another one won't change either point. If you accept the evidence as it stands, `/goal clear` ends the goal.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:27:57\n- **Source:** Cricket (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports (cricket) with a comedy story campaign. A TV camera behind the bowler for every delivery, a wide camera following the ball, close-ups and a side-on review camera; three-quarter view for story scenes.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio; tests on Node and Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's pixel-art characters at 320×240 (expanded), canvas lighting, engine shapes and materials, and new cricket assets.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, posed by IK for two-handed bat swings, the overarm bowling action and umpire signals.\n- **Audio:** Layered music, synthesized effects, a crowd engine and Animalese-style gibberish voices, all in code.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1: a parallel Super Over for 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\n- **Testing:** Headless engine (`game.advance`, `game.debug`), scripted playthroughs and CPU bot matches behind one command, Playwright browser checks (including emulated touch, gamepad and mouse input), and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** None beyond the plan, the engine handoff docs and kits, and the AI Hub README and example.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 46: roughly 26 gameplay or logic bugs, 7 visual problems, 6 balance problems, 4 unused pieces of content, and a few errors in my own tests.\n2. **How many were critical?** 8:\n   - a dead ball that never ended\n   - two scenes that could only finish once\n   - a misnamed dead-ball handler\n   - the camera aimed far off the ground\n   - an engine crash drawing the ground at the low camera angle\n   - long throws counted as overthrows\n   - a commentary crash in CPU-only matches\n3. **Most helpful test:** The forced-outcome scenarios, which run the real ball-by-ball code end to end.\n4. **Least helpful test:** The check that deliveries land where aimed; it mostly measured the simulation's step size.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The character rig; its pose step can be wrapped to add IK.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** A custom view stores its pitch in radians (`pitchDeg` holds the degrees). In a headless test, a long press left the click check empty.\n3. **Built myself:** The cricket simulation, fielding, running, umpiring and reviews, and the forced-outcome layer.\n4. **Hardest part:** The low TV camera: the ground drawing broke at that angle, and the far end needed a painted backdrop.\n5. **Changed:**\n   - a cricket bat with a two-handed grip\n   - batting pads, moustaches, beards and glasses\n   - PlayStation glyphs by default, with Xbox as the option\n   - Create + Options left to the AI Hub\n   - ten cached ground drawings instead of six\n   - a fix for the ground-drawing cache crash\n6. **One change:** A perspective (telephoto) camera option for ground views.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **Liked most:** The testable definition of done, and the freedom to change the engine.\n2. **Confusing:** How binding a very large plan is when TASK.md wins on disagreements.\n3. **Hardest:** Fitting the full game and its testing into one session.\n4. **Would change:** Give a target scope, and say which plan features are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2152,"cache_read_input_tokens":765730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2152},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"545d9604-3eac-4c35-9b61-7066df831e99","uuid":"e8892004-7ef3-4805-b485-bbb1509a28dc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:25:22.216Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7vzSUWrk1kAz46zaaE"}
